speechtext:
Of course it is the old story;
I assure my hon. friend that- there are always complaints. I hardly think he would suggest that for the sake of perhaps one business, important though it may be in that particular community, the department should maintain a customs house. If we had followed that principle we would not have closed any ports at all. In this instance, where the revenue 
amounted to $463, the salary of the collector was $1,020 per annum, so the port cost us a great deal more money than we received from it. However, I shall be very glad to make an investigation.
